# 21. Practical Implementation Principles

When designing browser automation infrastructure, several principles are useful.

### Give every environment an identity

A profile should be identifiable and associated with an account.

### Keep persistent state separated

Cookies, sessions, and other persistent data should remain associated with the correct environment.

### Separate configuration from secrets

Browser configuration should not require storing passwords or sensitive credentials directly in source code.

### Monitor browser health

A browser worker can fail independently of the account or network.

### Make recovery possible

A system should be able to determine which environment belongs to an account after a restart or failure.

### Avoid unnecessary changes

Stable, predictable environments are generally easier to operate than environments that are constantly modified.

